-- The 8 topics people pick when they join (approved by the owner on 16 Oct 2026) and the one main
-- topic of each sermon they cover. See supabase/migrations/20261016000300_topics.sql and
-- 20261016000500_topics_reader.sql.
--
-- How the tags were made (re-tuned after Argon's hand-check of 136 sermons, docs/topic-check):
-- 1. Embedding match: each sermon's passages are averaged and compared with each topic's match_text
--    (text-embedding-3-large, 768 dimensions), standardised per topic (z).
-- 2. AI reader: gpt-5.4-mini reads the title and seven transcript excerpts spread through the sermon
--    against written rules for each topic and names the main topic, or none.
-- 3. A sermon is tagged only when the reader's topic is one of its two best matches with z >= 0. Against
--    the hand-check that was right 91% of the time (the embedding alone 59%). 1,379 of the 2,769 sermons
--    with transcripts are tagged; the rest stay in the library and search, just not under a topic.
-- The tag rows below are the result, so re-running this file restores exactly this set. New sermons
-- are tagged with scripts/tag-topics.py (same reader and rule).

